  "description": "Change of use of first floor ancillary pub accommodation to 1 x 1-bed and 1x 3-bed self contained flats, involving single storey rear extension, alterations to fenestration and internal alterations",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "There is insufficient justification that the proposed change of use of the first floor ancillary pub accommodation to two self-contained flats would not compromise the operation or viability of the public house. In addition, there are concerns with the relationship between the proposed living accommodation and the public house and that the residential use without adequate noise mitigation could lead to future complaints requiring the public house to have to make improvements that may at that future date affect the viability of the public house. The proposal is contrary to Policy 16 of the Havering Local Plan and Policies HC7 and S1 of the London Plan.",
    "The proposed flats would, by reason of their insufficient internal floor space failing to meet the minimum internal floor space standards, result in substandard residential accommodation detrimental to the amenity of the future residents contrary to Policy 7 of the Havering Local Plan and Policy D6 of the London Plan.",
    "Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate whether the commercial use and associated impacts of the public house, including noise, vibration and disturbance, and the related land including the beer garden, plant and equipment, customer activity, deliveries and operational noise, including the use of amplified music equipment, would not result in a loss of amenity to future occupiers of the proposed self-contained flats. Furthermore, no suitable mitigation measures have been submitted to overcome these concerns. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies 7 and 34 of the Havering Local Plan, Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, notification of intended refusal and the reason(s) for it was given to Kyson Design Ltd via email on 9th June 2026."
  ],
